 `async (request) => response`, so callers choose HTTP, IPC or a fake.
 
-- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`. It follows the API's
+  `next_cursor` through all pages; the first request omits `cursor`, and each
+  returned cursor is sent unchanged on the next request. Pagination ends when
+  `next_cursor` is `null` or absent.
 - `getItem(transport, id)` → one item; rejects on any non-200 response.
 - `lowStock(items, threshold)` → SKUs with `qty` below the threshold.
 
